WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.680
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Arrow we found the Man Under The Hood doesn’t

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:13.830
matter and we got probably one of the most
important Island Flashbacks all season.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.150
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Arrow videos and Q&amp;As every week.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.700
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.980
I’m working on something special for the
next 4 weeks too.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.949
So let’s start with the title.

00:00:23.949 --> 00:00:25.670
The Man Under The Hood, what’s it all about?

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.340
That was our big question.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.480
When we found out someone’s identity was
being revealed I had all kinds of plot theories,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.180
which Quentyn answered in this really eloquent
speech.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.650
But let’s talk about that during my top
5 moments.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.630
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up.

00:00:38.630 --> 00:00:41.540
Here we go, Number 5 - Quentin’s Man Under
The Hood Speech.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.040
This is a version of the Dark Knight speech
that Gordon had in that movie.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.550
Which is fitting, because I always thought
there was a strong parallel between Quentyn

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:51.080
and The Arrow and Gordon and Batman.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:55.400
Maybe that means someday Quentyn might be
commissioner of Starling City?

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.390
This was such a great way to put Laurel into
this really positive mindset as to how she

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.720
was going deal with learning Oliver’s secret.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.320
And I love that Quentyn refused find out.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.980
I kind of suspected from the moment she found
out that she was going to treat this like

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.980
a good thing.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.710
Once the shock wore off.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.490
And that epic Hug she gives Oliver is her
just shedding her last moment of doubt.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.030
It was great, every time on Arrow should be
hug time.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:21.220
She’s definitely going to become another
stealth member of Team Arrow.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.520
In the way Quentyn is is an unofficial member.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:31.080
And side, note I definitely think we’ll
see a Slade Oliver Hug by the end of the season.

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.740
They wouldn’t create a cure if they weren’t
going to use it.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.390
Number 4 - Slade Is Waiting In The Arrow Cave

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.220
This was one of the best action sequences
all season.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.990
It’s almost like a short film, you could
just cut it out and post it as a 4 minute

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:48.270
trailer.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.480
Stephen Amell even did this funny thing on
twitter where he teased fans by giving a breakdown

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.480
of the scene.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.480
Here’s his post.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.780
I can’t wait to see him do a comedic role
someday.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:01.630
Unless you consider Oliver on Arrow to be
a comedic character.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.280
He and Felicity would make a great comedy
duo.

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.030
She already gets most of the comedic lines
in the scripts.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:11.930
Number 3 - Slade Is Using Roy To Create His
Army

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:16.400
Even though they’re not a legion of soldiers,
if one person on mirakuru is bad.

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.800
Even a couple of them would be a nightmare.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.860
And Roy in that crazy Tanning Booth looking
harness was straight out of a horror movie.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.310
I love how this episode kind of jumped from
noir cop drama to science fiction at star

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:30.120
labs to horror in Slade’s lab.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.599
Which is really a credit to the writing and
the set design.

00:02:32.599 --> 00:02:35.500
I’m guessing that when Roy skipped town
Slade captured him.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.790
Roy didn’t turn sides.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.120
If it wasn’t clear, Roy still has Mirakuru
in him.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:46.800
He flips out in the next episode, so we know
he wakes up off that table in the Arrow cave.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.400
The way the mirakuru works I think is that
the serum is like a catalyst for your body’s

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.710
own natural abilities.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:56.860
So once you get injected, your own body just
starts producing it.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:03.170
That’s why Roy’s blood can create all
those other super soldiers and Slade can transfuse

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:05.140
Isabel into a super soldier.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.670
Number 2 - There Is A Cure For The Mirakuru

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:10.950
This was one of the biggest Island Flashback
scenes ever.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.420
Just because it gave us the solution to the
problem that is Slade.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.780
We’re going to make him human again, there’s
a big asterisk though.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:23.660
When Ivo was explaining the cure, he said
it only reverses the physiological effects

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.000
of the Mirakuru.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.330
Not the psychological, and it seems like the
only reason Slade is attacking Oliver is because

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.250
of evil Tinkerbell Shado.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:36.239
So if they cure him, it sounds like it won’t
get her out of Slade’s mind.

00:03:36.239 --> 00:03:39.709
I may have just heard it wrong, but either
way he won’t be indestructable anymore.

00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:41.730
They’ll be able to kill him for real.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.870
Meaning Oliver is probably going to have a
choice to make like he did back on the Island.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.650
He’ll either have to Kill Slade or do something
else.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:49.910
I keep saying that Oliver is trying to not
kill people this season, so I don’t think

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.910
he’ll end up killing Slade.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.540
For a number of reasons, but that doesn’t
mean Sara won’t try.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.040
Like a reversal of how Oliver killed Ivo.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.170
She might try to take care of Slade for Oliver.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:02.489
and my Number 1 moment - The Flash Crossover
with Cisco Ramon and Caitlin Snow

00:04:02.489 --> 00:04:07.250
So much to talk about here, let’s stick
to the big stuff.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.380
First off, the Star Labs facility they’re
working at is like the candy store of Super

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.380
Weapons.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:16.099
In case you missed it, when they grab that
gun Caitlin says all of the tech in that locked

00:04:16.099 --> 00:04:20.299
area belonged to Arthur Light who was Doctor
Light in the comics.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:23.749
A super looney tunes bad guy.

00:04:23.749 --> 00:04:26.280
I think we can thank Geoff Johns for including
the name drop.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:32.809
He wrote the Flash comic book for a long time
and is working on the Flash TV Show right

00:04:32.809 --> 00:04:36.339
now, so it makes sense that he would write
this episode.

00:04:36.339 --> 00:04:40.949
They also answered everyone’s future crossover
questions when they mentioned Felicity visiting

00:04:40.949 --> 00:04:41.949
Barry.

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:44.610
He’s being kept in Star Labs Central City
facility.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.199
The producers confirmed he wouldn’t wake
up until the first episode of The Flash.

00:04:48.199 --> 00:05:04.669
Which is done, yes they’ve finished the
pilot.

00:05:04.669 --> 00:05:09.270
Geoff Johns, Andrew Kreisberg and Marc Guggenheim
tweeted this picture when they watched it

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.400
for the first time.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.189
No word on when we’ll get to see it.

00:05:13.189 --> 00:05:16.869
Hopefully they’ll just air it on TV after
the Arrow finale in 5 weeks.

00:05:16.869 --> 00:05:24.629
and here’s one giant bonus WTF Moment - Slade
brings Isabel back to life by transfusing

00:05:24.629 --> 00:05:25.689
Mirakuru into her.

00:05:25.689 --> 00:05:29.639
Andrew Kreisberg just revealed a whole bunch
of details about her character.

00:05:29.639 --> 00:05:34.059
She’s basically a mashup of Isabel Rochev
and Ravager.

00:05:34.059 --> 00:05:39.669
So she has Isabel’s backstory from the comics,
she was Oliver’s father’s lover and wanted

00:05:39.669 --> 00:05:40.699
revenge on his family.

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:44.009
And the tv show is turning her into Ravager.

00:05:44.009 --> 00:05:47.689
The way Slade was looking at her on the table
was kind of the way a father would look at

00:05:47.689 --> 00:05:48.689
a daughter.

00:05:48.689 --> 00:05:56.249
So maybe he kind of thinks of her as his adopted
daughter in a really perverse way.

00:05:56.249 --> 00:06:02.529
We’ve all seen the pictures of her as Ravager,
but now we know that she’ll be juiced up

00:06:02.529 --> 00:06:03.800
on mirakuru.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:10.559
So Summer Glau is essentially playing a Terminator
again, and it’s going to be full of awesome.

00:06:10.559 --> 00:06:11.559
You have no idea.

00:06:11.559 --> 00:06:15.440
There was this other really cool bit of information
about the Ravager persona they revealed.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:23.729
On the show, they originally wanted Caity
Lotz’s Sara character to start as Ravager

00:06:23.729 --> 00:06:28.909
and switch back to being good, until Summer
Glau was cast.

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:35.339
Because she worked so well as a fighter, they
decided to give the Ravager arc to Isabel.

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:39.399
So now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was.

00:06:39.399 --> 00:06:44.460
Flash Crossover, Laurel kind of becoming part
of the Arrow fan club or that Ravager teaser

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:45.460
at the end?

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:49.990
Overall the episode was a solid A. I feel
like I’m going to be giving straight A’s

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.009
to all the rest of the episodes this season.

00:06:52.009 --> 00:06:55.629
The show has done such a good job of building
momentum.

00:06:55.629 --> 00:06:59.899
Which is amazing considering how awesome The
Promise was earlier this year.

00:06:59.899 --> 00:07:03.460
Stephen Amell had this really nice rally cry
for the next 5 weeks so I’m even going to

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:07.060
be doing a special countdown series I’ll
explain in a sec.

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.999
I know I mentioned how the episode went from
cop drama to sci fi to horror, and that’s

00:07:08.999 --> 00:07:13.150
one of the reasons why I think the show is
able to stay so interesting.

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.580
It’s really easy to get comfortable with
a format, like just watching your billionth

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.720
episode of Law and Order.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.339
I’m really interested to see which genres
they do in the rest of the episodes this season.

00:07:23.339 --> 00:07:25.919
And I’m really coming around on Laurel’s
character.

00:07:25.919 --> 00:07:29.559
I know everyone is still thinking she’s
going to become Black Canary in season 3,

00:07:29.559 --> 00:07:31.399
but I still think that’s too soon.

00:07:31.399 --> 00:07:34.300
I think she’s just going to stay in her
current role and just start trying to help

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:39.090
Team Arrow from behind her desk, the same
way Quentyn helps them via the police force.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:42.469
The character that’s really dangling in
the wind right now is Thea, John Barrowman

00:07:42.469 --> 00:07:45.840
probably won’t be back till the finale,
but she is a big part of Roy’s arc next

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:46.840
week.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:51.409
So she hasn’t completey skipped town.

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:54.189
I feel like I’ve covered all the important
stuff, but let me know what your final thoughts

00:07:54.189 --> 00:07:59.369
are on the episode and whether or not you
think Oliver will be able to cure Slade.

00:07:59.369 --> 00:08:01.710
Just like normal, my Q&amp;A will post tomorrow.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:05.669
Be sure to subscribe to get it if you’re
finding me for the first time.

00:08:05.669 --> 00:08:07.759
That countdown series I mentioned will start
next Wednesday morning.

00:08:07.759 --> 00:08:11.119
I’m going to do bonus morning videos for
Arrow every wednesday just to help get everyone

00:08:11.119 --> 00:08:13.479
pumped for the finale.

00:08:13.479 --> 00:08:17.229
Feel free to suggest topics in the comments.

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:21.149
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A, i’ll
add the annotation as soon as I post it and

00:08:21.149 --> 00:08:22.569
click here for last week’s episode.

00:08:22.569 --> 00:08:24.220
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:24.689
High Fives!

